#========= DWBA input — collective inelastic scattering (p,p')
# 40Ca(p,p')40Ca exciting the 3- state at 3.737 MeV. The trailing token after the
# potential is the deformation length (beta) for the collective form factor.
#
# NOTE: the DWBA *expansion* below is faithful to Cleopatra (PARAMETERSET
# ineloca2, BETA=...), but PtolemyCpp's collective-inelastic engine keys off the
# BELX = B(EL) reduced transition probability rather than the deformation length,
# so this deck currently expands but does not run to a cross section. It is
# included to document the inelastic input syntax.
#reaction         gs-Jpi  orbital  Jpi(Ex)  Ex      ELab     Potentials  beta
40Ca(p,p)40Ca     0+      none     3-       3.737   30MeV    K           1.0
